# A TMS cascade withdraws in cause order ([RFCS.7a.4]). See
# fixtures/128_cascade_order.ds.
#
#   pump 1   Seed k1 (fact 0) derives Made (1), which derives Shipped (2)
#   pump 2   G k1 is blocked by `no Shipped`
#   pump 3   C c1 with y = 0 arrives while `watch`'s C node has no left token
#   retract  the Seed: Made loses its justifier and is withdrawn; that ends
#            Shipped's, so Shipped is withdrawn; that releases (g), and
#            `c.x / c.y` traps
#
# The retract is the case: each cascaded withdrawal is recorded before what
# its own evaluation produces, so Made's FactWithdraw precedes Shipped's and
# Shipped's precedes the fault. The recordings check compares the
# FactWithdraw fact ids, which the trace's bare `retract` lines cannot. The
# vector RFCS.7a.4_cascade_withdraws_in_cause_order pins the order against
# the clause.
assert Seed k="k1"
pump
assert G k="k1"
pump
assert C id="c1" x=1 y=0
pump
retract 0
pump
